From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Give IOMMU1 the display engine
 port gate

A master's register block in the IOMMU does not answer while the
master's port on the MBUS matrix is gated, and the access stalls the
bus. The IOMMU driver takes a reference on the port gate of a master,
given as a "masterN" clock, for as long as the master translates. The
A733 clock driver marks these gates CLK_IS_CRITICAL, so they stay
enabled and the reference does not change their state.

Name the port gate of the display engine, master 2 of the second IOMMU
(manual chapter 10). Its MBUS port is DESYS, bit 11 of
MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING_REG (manual section 4.1.6.83). The display engine
top driver takes a reference on that gate, but only from its probe to its
unbind.
The IOMMU is built in and touches the master's block when it attaches
the master at boot, on a flush, on a fault and on resume, also before a
modular display driver has bound and after the driver has unbound.

Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S: with the port gates of the video engine
cleared, the first unmap through its masters stalls the bus until the
watchdog resets the SoC.

Nothing changes until a node lists the IOMMU in "iommus": the driver
enables a master clock only for a master with a user.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: on two boards the IOMMU holds the display
engine's port gate from boot, before the display driver binds, while
master 2 translates.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 334d5880d32f..384e13a004b3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1037,9 +1037,10 @@ iommu1: iommu@3910000 {
 				 <&ccu CLK_AHB_IOMMU1_SYS>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU1>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC0_GATE>,
-				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC0_GATE>;
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC0_GATE>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_DESYS>;
 			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus",
-				      "master0", "master1";
+				      "master0", "master1", "master2";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_IOMMU1_SYS>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 		};
